>## Run a parser and pair its result with the source span it consumed. The span starts at the first codepoint the parser consumed and ends at the end of the last token it completed (see markTokenEnd), so trailing whitespace and comments are excluded.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term spanned = λp.let parse := λinput.cases(parsing.ParseResult){success=λs.let start := parsing.ParseInput[offset] input in let end := ordering.max start (parsing.ParseInput[tokenEnd] (parsing.ParseSuccess[remainder] s)) in parsing.ParseResult{success = parsing.ParseSuccess{value = (parsing.ParseSuccess[value] s, parsing.SourceSpan{start = start, end = end}), remainder = parsing.ParseSuccess[remainder] s}}, failure=λe.parsing.ParseResult{failure = e}} (parsing.Parser[] p input) in wrap(parsing.Parser){parse}
